.L20089:
    .string "requires"
.L20090:
    .string "special-form"
.L20091:
    .string "(requires condition)"
.L20092:
    .string "Precondition, checked on entry: a false condition raises E_CONTRACT_VIOLATION. The condition may only compute; I/O, foreign calls, actors, state changes or exit in it, or in what it calls, are E_CONTRACT_EFFECT."
.L20093:
    .string "ensures"
.L20094:
    .string "special-form"
.L20095:
    .string "(ensures condition)"
.L20096:
    .string "Postcondition, checked after the body; `result` is the return value. Pure like `requires` (E_CONTRACT_EFFECT)."
.L20097:
    .string "invariant"
.L20098:
    .string "special-form"
.L20099:
    .string "(invariant condition)"
.L20100:
    .string "Checked where written, like `requires`, and pure like it (E_CONTRACT_EFFECT)."
.L20101:
    .string "contracts"
.L20102:
    .string "special-form"
.L20103:
    .string "(contracts profile form)"
.L20104:
    .string "Compile `form` (or, bare, the next top-level form) under a contract profile: strict, debug, warn, off or production."
.L20105:
    .string "recover"
.L20106:
    .string "special-form"
.L20107:
    .string "(recover body ((E_CODE) fallback) ((String) fallback) ...)"
.L20108:
    .string "`body`, or the fallback of the first arm matching the error: an E_ code by message prefix, a type name or `_` for any."
.L20109:
    .string "checkpoint"
.L20110:
    .string "special-form"
.L20111:
    .string "(checkpoint expr)"
.L20112:
    .string "`expr`; if it raises, the outer let-mut variables it assigned are restored before the error propagates."
.L20114:
    .string "test"
.L20115:
    .string "special-form"
.L20116:
    .string "(test \"name\" body (:expect-panic true))"
.L20117:
    .string "One test case. With `(:expect-panic true)` the body must raise: raising passes, and returning normally fails with \"expected a panic, but the test body returned normally\"."
.L20118:
    .string "test-suite"
.L20119:
    .string "special-form"
.L20120:
    .string "(test-suite \"name\" item ...)"
.L20121:
    .string "Top level. Groups tests, nested suites and test-property forms; they register as `name/test`, each run between the suite's setup and teardown forms."
.L20122:
    .string "assert-equal"
.L20123:
    .string "special-form"
.L20124:
    .string "(assert-equal actual expected)"
.L20125:
    .string "Assert two values are equal."
.L20126:
    .string "assert-true"
.L20127:
    .string "special-form"
.L20128:
    .string "(assert-true expr)"
.L20129:
    .string "Assert a value is true."
.L20130:
    .string "assert-false"
.L20131:
    .string "special-form"
.L20132:
    .string "(assert-false expr)"
.L20133:
    .string "Assert a value is false."
.L20134:
    .string "assert-fail"
.L20135:
    .string "special-form"
.L20136:
    .string "(assert-fail expr \"message\")"
.L20137:
    .string "Fails unless evaluating `expr` raises an error; the message is optional."
.L20138:
    .string "test-property"
.L20139:
    .string "special-form"
.L20140:
    .string "(test-property \"name\" gen-int (fn (x) bool))"
.L20141:
    .string "Runs the property (one to three parameters) over the generator's fixed samples: gen-int, gen-bool, gen-string or gen-float. Fails naming the first rejected sample."
.L20142:
    .string "test-compile"
.L20143:
    .string "special-form"
.L20144:
    .string "(test-compile expr (:expect-error true))"
.L20145:
    .string "Top level. Decided at compile time: a test that passes when `expr` compiles, or with :expect-error true, when it does not."
.L20146:
    .string "setup"
.L20147:
    .string "special-form"
.L20148:
    .string "(setup expr ...)"
.L20149:
    .string "Inside a test-suite: runs before each of its tests."
.L20150:
    .string "teardown"
.L20151:
    .string "special-form"
.L20152:
    .string "(teardown expr ...)"
.L20153:
    .string "Inside a test-suite: runs after each of its tests, also when the test fails."
.L20154:
    .string "run-tests"
.L20155:
    .string "special-form"
.L20156:
    .string "(run-tests (:filter \"text\"))"
.L20157:
    .string "Run every `test` registered so far, or with :filter only those whose names contain the text, one at a time in registration order, and report."
